Level 2 : Make Work Observable (start job → track lifecycle → react to updates)
Learnings : 
# Backend becomes the Source of Truth (Frontend repeatly ask what is the status and backend answers)
# Starting work ≠ finishing work (This single idea changes how large systems are designed)
# We separate TRIGGER from OBSERVATION (2 responsibilties : start the job / Watch the job)(Different API's for both)
# Polling is asking reality repeatedly
# Life Cycle thinking (Every Task is divided into phases)(idle->running->success/failed)(Everything builds upon lifecycle.)

Background Job Architecture:
Task Store (Source of Truth): dictionary for now -> later real Database
Start API -> Job Manager (Creates Task ID and triggers Worker) -> Worker Does the Work (Updates Status)-> Status API (Sends Status of main job to frontend) 


